{
  "name": "firefly",
  "_about": "The common eastern firefly (Photinus pyralis), 1.2 cm long: long, soft and flattened; the pronotum a broad SHIELD hiding the head from above, yellow with a black centre spot and a pink patch to each side; soft dark wing cases edged pale yellow at the sides and down the seam; big eyes; dark thread antennae; the last segments of the abdomen the pale yellow-green lantern underneath. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/beetles.py on insectlib.py (six jointed legs on a tripod gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
